WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:05.044
This is the RusNITI institute building in Chelyabinsk.

2
00:00:05.224 --> 00:00:13.074
The institute was established in 1961 as a research and
technology centre for the pipe industry.

3
00:00:13.254 --> 00:00:20.549
Its specialists develop and study new pipe products and improve
manufacturing processes and equipment.

4
00:00:20.729 --> 00:00:28.088
Before your visit begins, let us explain the health and safety
rules that will help keep you safe throughout your visit.

5
00:00:29.517 --> 00:00:32.823
Welcome to RusNITI and TMK.

6
00:00:33.003 --> 00:00:35.626
Your safety is our priority.

7
00:00:35.806 --> 00:00:41.480
Please take a moment to learn the essential rules for a safe
visit to the institute.

8
00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:46.240
Before your visit, complete the safety induction.

9
00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:50.120
A safety specialist will explain the safety rules.

10
00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:55.546
Confirm that you have completed the induction by signing the
registration log.

11
00:00:56.917 --> 00:01:01.022
The same site rules apply throughout the grounds and buildings.

12
00:01:01.202 --> 00:01:04.892
Stay out of areas you are not authorised to enter.

13
00:01:05.072 --> 00:01:07.418
Observe all warning signs.

14
00:01:07.598 --> 00:01:10.765
Enter production areas only with permission.

15
00:01:12.117 --> 00:01:19.007
Test rigs, chemical laboratories, electrical installations and
cranes present increased risks.

16
00:01:19.187 --> 00:01:26.109
Entry without authorisation and the required personal protective
equipment is strictly prohibited.

17
00:01:27.483 --> 00:01:33.177
The safety specialist provides your personal protective
equipment during the induction.

18
00:01:33.357 --> 00:01:37.400
It is mandatory in production and laboratory areas.

19
00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:40.225
Check that it is in good condition.

20
00:01:40.405 --> 00:01:43.123
Keep it on until you leave the area.

21
00:01:43.303 --> 00:01:46.800
Report any damage to your escort immediately.

22
00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:52.501
Do not touch test samples, control panels or safety guards.

23
00:01:52.681 --> 00:01:55.582
Keep a safe distance during testing.

24
00:01:55.762 --> 00:02:00.829
Samples can break and fragments can be thrown out suddenly,
without warning.

25
00:02:02.183 --> 00:02:09.830
If an alarm sounds, stop what you are doing, listen to your
escort and follow the indicated evacuation route.

26
00:02:10.010 --> 00:02:14.287
If someone is injured or chemicals are spilled, alert staff.

27
00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:18.061
Do not try to deal with the incident on your own.

28
00:02:19.417 --> 00:02:21.773
Your induction is complete.

29
00:02:21.953 --> 00:02:26.806
Confirm that you understand the rules by signing the
registration log.

30
00:02:26.986 --> 00:02:30.357
Your escort will guide you along a safe route.

31
00:02:30.537 --> 00:02:33.300
Thank you for following the safety rules.

32
00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:41.583
For safety matters, contact the Technical Director or the
occupational health and safety specialist.

33
00:02:41.763 --> 00:02:45.761
We wish you a safe and productive time at the institute.
